  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Singh Kushwah vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 29 November, 2019 Author: Sheel Nagu Bench: Sheel Nagu 1 M.Cr.C. No.46081/2019 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh M.Cr.C. No.46081/2019 (Anil Singh Kushwah Vs. State of M.P.) Gwalior, Dated : 29.11.2019",
    "facts": "The applicant has been arrested on 24.08.2019 by Police Station Gohad, District Bhind in connection with Crime No.306/2019 registered in relation to the offences punishable u/S.420, 272 and 273 of IPC and u/Ss.51, 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Learned Public Prosecutor for the State opposed the application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of bail is made out. This is first application under Section 439 Cr.P.C where allegation is that at the shop of the applicant, certain material used for adulteration of milk and making of synthetic milk were found including caustic soda, detergent powder and hydrogen peroxide etc.",
    "arguments": "This order will remain operative subject to compliance of the following conditions by the applicant :- 1. The applicant will comply with all the terms and conditions of the bond executed by him; 2. The applicant will cooperate in the investigation/trial, as the case may be; 3. The applicant will not indulge himself in extending inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to the Police Officer, as the case may be; 4. The applicant shall not commit an offence similar to the offence of which he is accused; 5. The applicant will not seek unnecessary adjournments during the trial; and 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "This order will remain operative subject to compliance of the following conditions by the applicant :- 1. The applicant will comply with all the terms and conditions of the bond executed by him; 2. The applicant will cooperate in the investigation/trial, as the case may be; 3. The applicant will not indulge himself in extending inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to the Police Officer, as the case may be; 4. The applicant shall not commit an offence similar to the offence of which he is accused; 5. The applicant will not seek unnecessary adjournments during the trial; and 6."
